        <body>
            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0550" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/10191: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-22T20:00:00+09:00">September 22, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 22—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>405. Lieutenant Layton,<anchor n="44" xml:id="d605-f1"/> Assistant Naval Attaché,
                    has submitted to me the following memorandum dated today: <pb facs="0551"
                        n="544" xml:id="pg544"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Memorandum for Ambassador. The Senior Aide to the Navy Minister, Captain
                            Kondo, called at 11:40 a.m. today and stated as follows:</p>
                        <p>The Japanese Navy Department has received a report from Admiral Hasegawa
                            to the effect that reliable information indicates the Chinese are
                            planning to bomb foreign Embassies and Legations in Nanking using a
                            plane (or planes) painted and marked to resemble Japanese air craft in
                            order to instigate foreign nations’ participation in the present
                            conflict.</p>
                        <p>When asked if such planes (being foreign models) would not be readily
                            recognized as non-Japanese types he said some Chinese planes closely
                            resembled Japanese models. Comment: This is open to question.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
